// PLAN:
// DEPTH_FIRST_SCREENS: ['library_home', 'journey_reader']
// Reason: 'library_home' is the critical entry point establishing the quiet, dignified tone and the core search interaction; 'journey_reader' is the "aha" moment where cold data becomes a human narrative with inflection highlighting.
//
// COMPONENTS:
// - App (Root, state router, theme provider, demo controls)
// - TeamsTabChrome / SharePointDocumentChrome (Layout wrappers)
// - Toast (Non-blocking notifications)
// - LibraryHome (Search input, rotating placeholders, featured rail with Imagen)
// - SearchResults (3 cards, confidence bands, AI rationale tooltips)
// - JourneyReader (Narrative synthesis, scroll-triggered inflection highlight, sparkline, margin tags)
// - ReflectionJournal (AI prompt, text area, timeline of past entries)
// - UnmaskConnect (FERPA consent table, AI scaffold drawer, AI FERPA check)
// - LizDashboard (Heatmap grid, AI gap analysis, outreach generator)
//
// STATE:
// - currentScreen (string)
// - quietMode (boolean)
// - searchQuery (string)
// - searchResults (array)
// - selectedFootprintId (string)
// - savedFootprints (array of IDs)
// - reflectionEntries (array of objects)
// - toasts (array)
//
// AI ENDPOINTS:
// 1. ai_semantic_search (Gemini fallback) -> library_home
// 2. ai_narrative_synthesis (Claude fallback + VS) -> journey_reader
// 3. ai_inflection_detection (Gemini fallback) -> journey_reader
// 4. ai_reflection_prompt (Claude fallback + VS) -> reflection_journal
// 5. ai_conversation_scaffold (Claude fallback + VS) -> unmask_connect
// 6. ai_ferpa_classifier (Claude fallback) -> unmask_connect
// 7. ai_coverage_gap_analysis (Gemini fallback + VS) -> liz_dashboard
